STUDY ABSTRACT:
OBJECTIVE To evaluate the performance of a new Chlamydia Rapid Test with vaginal swab specimens as a potential tool for 
chlamydia diagnosis and screening. DESIGN Performance evaluation study. Settings A young people's sexual health centre 
(site 1) and two genitourinary medicine clinics (sites 2 and 3) in the United Kingdom. PARTICIPANTS 1349 women aged 
between 16 and 54 attending one of the three clinics. MAIN OUTCOME MEASURES Sensitivity, specificity, positive 
predictive value, and negative predictive value of the Chlamydia Rapid Test versus polymerase chain reaction and strand 
